# SRG-APP-000095-AU-000680  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must produce audit records containing information
# to establish what type of events occurred.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000095-AU-000680
group:           V-221908
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000130
control_rev5:    AU-3

contribution:    Splunk stamps every indexed record with the sourcetype assigned to its
                 input, which is the record's event type, and its own audit records reach a
                 searchable index when the audit trail is queued to the index.

governs:         audit.conf - The audit trail Splunk keeps of its own activity, and how those records
                 are signed.
governs:         inputs.conf - Configures inputs, distributed inputs such as forwarders, and file system
                 monitoring.

check:           inputs.conf [] sourcetype non_empty
check:           audit.conf [auditTrail] queueing not_equals false

external:        The originating hosts and devices must emit an event type or category in
                 the records they transmit; Splunk classifies what it receives and cannot
                 add a type the sender omitted.

citation:        OVER-REACH and INVENTION. Removed eventtypes.conf [<eventtype>] search
                 non_empty: the shipped eventtypes.conf declares "search =" empty in its
                 default stanza and ships no event types, so the condition fails a stock
                 instance that nonetheless stamps a sourcetype on every record; event types
                 are an optional search-time classification feature and neither the check
                 nor the fix text requires them. Also removed props.conf [<spec>] <spec>
                 present, which named the spec-file placeholder as both stanza and key:
                 props.conf has no setting of that name, so the condition could never
                 match, and the determined row is a whole-file presence test that every
                 installation passes.
finding:         Splunk does not establish the type of each record it holds - inputs have
                 no sourcetype assigned, or the audit trail is not queued to an index - so
                 the event type cannot be determined from the stored records.
